course: dictionary
lesson: 2097
title: A word for huge lands
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A continent is one of the very large areas of land on Earth. Use the words around it to help you. «Frogs live on every continent except Antarctica» tells you that a continent is a place where frogs can live, and that Antarctica is one of them.
explain: Numbers in the sentence give you another clue. «Asia is the largest continent, with about 44 million square kilometres» shows that a continent is measured by its area, so it is a huge piece of land, much bigger than a country.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. In Britain, «the Continent» with a capital letter usually means mainland Europe. Read the whole sentence and the sentences near it to find which meaning the writer wants.
fact: A continent is one of the very large areas of land on Earth.
fact: Most people count seven continents: Africa, Antarctica, Asia, Australia (Oceania), Europe, North America and South America.
fact: Asia is the biggest continent and has the most people, while Antarctica is the coldest.
fact: Countries belong to continents: Canada is in North America.
fact: The continents move very slowly, about as fast as fingernails grow.
exercise: «Frogs live on every continent except Antarctica.» Which continent has no frogs living on it? | Africa | Asia | Europe | *Antarctica
exercise: «Asia is the largest continent.» According to the text, which continent is the largest? | *Asia | North America | Africa | Europe
exercise: How many continents do most people count? | Six | *Seven | Five | Nine
test: Ella reads, «In Britain, the Continent means mainland Europe.» What does the Continent mean in Britain? | An island near Britain | *Mainland Europe | Every country on Earth | The sea floor
test: Which continent is the coldest, with no permanent towns? | Asia | *Antarctica | Australia (Oceania) | South America
exam: Canada is in which continent? | *North America | Europe | Africa | Asia
